WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.883
- He's been looking after himself

00:00:01.883 --> 00:00:03.947
since he was 14 years old.

00:00:03.947 --> 00:00:06.855
He partnered with Jay Z to
create Roc-A-Fella Records

00:00:06.855 --> 00:00:09.319
and changed the hip-hop industry.

00:00:09.319 --> 00:00:10.927
He's been involved in businesses

00:00:10.927 --> 00:00:13.385
from clothing, to films, to cars.

00:00:13.385 --> 00:00:17.777
He's Damon Dash and here are
his top ten rules for success.

00:00:17.777 --> 00:00:20.695
(aircraft thundering)

00:00:20.695 --> 00:00:22.415
- Nine to fives aren't good because

00:00:22.415 --> 00:00:24.665
you hustling for a weekend.

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:27.999
But when you do something
that's for yourself

00:00:27.999 --> 00:00:31.540
and your family, it never feels like work.

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:35.611
I hustle for my last name,
I don't hustle for my first.

00:00:35.611 --> 00:00:37.886
I've learnt over the years,

00:00:37.886 --> 00:00:39.934
that with anything you have to be patient.

00:00:39.934 --> 00:00:41.619
Not five years patient,

00:00:41.619 --> 00:00:44.327
or five months patient,

00:00:44.327 --> 00:00:46.216
you could be ten years
patient if you want.

00:00:46.216 --> 00:00:49.233
Empire's aren't built overnight.

00:00:49.233 --> 00:00:50.504
I always tell everyone the Great Wall

00:00:50.504 --> 00:00:52.546
was a 2,000 year old plan.

00:00:52.546 --> 00:00:56.829
2,000, you know how many
lifetimes that is in one plan?

00:00:56.829 --> 00:00:59.095
And getting people

00:00:59.095 --> 00:01:01.587
to do the same, to have
the same exact agenda

00:01:01.587 --> 00:01:02.754
for lifetimes,

00:01:03.593 --> 00:01:06.509
for generations, that's crazy.

00:01:06.509 --> 00:01:07.968
So, you have to be patient when you want

00:01:07.968 --> 00:01:11.906
to do something
significant, no matter what.

00:01:11.906 --> 00:01:13.066
A lot of time that means

00:01:13.066 --> 00:01:17.233
not reaping the benefits
of something immediately.

00:01:18.276 --> 00:01:19.874
And that's the test.

00:01:19.874 --> 00:01:21.668
I don't think my approach on business

00:01:21.668 --> 00:01:23.735
is what the average person would advise.

00:01:23.735 --> 00:01:25.971
I hear people say, "Never
put up your own money,"

00:01:25.971 --> 00:01:27.328
and I'm saying put your own money up.

00:01:27.328 --> 00:01:28.525
Work harder than everyone, be patient

00:01:28.525 --> 00:01:30.702
and just know that if you're
going to do something on your own,

00:01:30.702 --> 00:01:32.622
you're going to have to feel some pain.

00:01:32.622 --> 00:01:36.274
You always have to have something
that's paying your bills.

00:01:36.274 --> 00:01:38.318
So that whatever you're
creating can breathe,

00:01:38.318 --> 00:01:39.676
so you don't have to rush it,

00:01:39.676 --> 00:01:42.575
you don't have to push it to
make money when it's not ready.

00:01:42.575 --> 00:01:45.498
You kind of always have
to have something solid,

00:01:45.498 --> 00:01:49.356
that's paying your bills,
'cause even as an artist,

00:01:49.356 --> 00:01:51.992
to me as a man, you still
have the responsibility

00:01:51.992 --> 00:01:53.511
to take care of your woman,

00:01:53.511 --> 00:01:57.655
to take care of your children,
and to take care of yourself.

00:01:57.655 --> 00:01:59.057
And you know, almost in that order,

00:01:59.057 --> 00:02:00.817
it's like children, your
woman, and then yourself.

00:02:00.817 --> 00:02:02.150
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:03.918
All of that should be taken care of.

00:02:03.918 --> 00:02:05.500
That's a real man.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:06.608
And as an artist, you can't say,

00:02:06.608 --> 00:02:08.496
"All right, well, I'm not going
to take care of my children,

00:02:08.496 --> 00:02:12.390
or take care of my woman, or
even take care of myself well

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:13.924
to protect my artistry."

00:02:13.924 --> 00:02:16.377
Then that's not artistry to
me, that's just being lazy.

00:02:16.377 --> 00:02:20.384
I think, as an artist, you have
to fight for that artistry.

00:02:20.384 --> 00:02:23.755
You have to figure out
how to pay your bills,

00:02:23.755 --> 00:02:26.000
so that the artistry can breathe.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:30.827
It also, you know, that's
how you feel like a real man.

00:02:30.827 --> 00:02:32.681
Have you ever watched a James Bond movie

00:02:32.681 --> 00:02:34.410
where it doesn't look like
he's losing at some point?

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:35.243
And then he wins.

00:02:35.243 --> 00:02:37.238
Or Batman, or Iron Man, or any superhero?

00:02:37.238 --> 00:02:40.843
There has to be some diversity
for you to overcome, to win.

00:02:40.843 --> 00:02:42.951
You can't be a champ
unless you're in a place

00:02:42.951 --> 00:02:44.620
where you look like you're
going to lose and then you win.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:47.319
The pain that's going to
come with being independent,

00:02:47.319 --> 00:02:49.493
you have to embrace it
because it's going to happen.

00:02:49.493 --> 00:02:51.011
Also know that the more
successful you get,

00:02:51.011 --> 00:02:52.442
the more problems you're going to have.

00:02:52.442 --> 00:02:53.877
The more knots you're
going to have to untie.

00:02:53.877 --> 00:02:55.597
Being a boss does not mean smooth sailing,

00:02:55.597 --> 00:02:56.591
it means having the ability

00:02:56.591 --> 00:02:58.186
to care about other people before yourself

00:02:58.186 --> 00:03:00.613
and to untie problems, untie knots.

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:01.641
That's all it is.

00:03:01.641 --> 00:03:03.646
It's not business if there's not problems.

00:03:03.646 --> 00:03:05.247
There's nothing good without struggle,

00:03:05.247 --> 00:03:06.442
it just doesn't happen.

00:03:06.442 --> 00:03:07.708
In all my experiences,

00:03:07.708 --> 00:03:09.758
there hasn't been one thing
that's been successful

00:03:09.758 --> 00:03:12.693
without me feeling some pain
before it was successful.

00:03:12.693 --> 00:03:14.634
So now, when there is pain, I embrace it.

00:03:14.634 --> 00:03:16.439
I've been embracing it, I'm a G about it,

00:03:16.439 --> 00:03:18.123
because I know must
mean, that if I'm cool,

00:03:18.123 --> 00:03:21.278
that what awaits me is the
darkness before the dawn.

00:03:21.278 --> 00:03:22.594
I don't want to sound corny

00:03:22.594 --> 00:03:25.315
but that's really what has to happen.

00:03:25.315 --> 00:03:26.983
I'm always going to play fair,

00:03:26.983 --> 00:03:30.343
I don't believe in doing
anything, unless it's fair,

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:33.206
because I believe there are
always karmic repercussions

00:03:33.206 --> 00:03:34.796
from doing things unfair,

00:03:34.796 --> 00:03:36.555
so what can appear to be a win,

00:03:36.555 --> 00:03:38.759
or something that appears
to be a fast, you know,

00:03:38.759 --> 00:03:42.821
fast money, I know in the
long run I'm going to suffer.

00:03:42.821 --> 00:03:44.292
That it's always a test.

00:03:44.292 --> 00:03:46.297
Anything quick is a test.

00:03:46.297 --> 00:03:47.731
I can get it quick if
I don't have to cheat,

00:03:47.731 --> 00:03:50.226
but if I've got to cheat to get it fast,

00:03:50.226 --> 00:03:51.499
I don't want it.

00:03:51.499 --> 00:03:54.743
My parents haven't bought me
clothes since I was about 14.

00:03:54.743 --> 00:03:57.662
I haven't had nobody buy
me nothing, let's say that.

00:03:57.662 --> 00:04:00.238
No one's taken care of me
since I was 14 years old.

00:04:00.238 --> 00:04:01.390
And I didn't want nobody taking care of me

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:02.747
'cause they couldn't.

00:04:02.747 --> 00:04:05.255
What they was trying to buy
me, I wasn't trying to wear.

00:04:05.255 --> 00:04:07.755
Taste, talent, and work ethic.

00:04:09.869 --> 00:04:10.702
I need all of it.

00:04:10.702 --> 00:04:12.869
Taste, talent, work ethic,

00:04:15.526 --> 00:04:17.359
you know, perspective.

00:04:18.242 --> 00:04:22.756
So when I interview, or even
when the people I work with

00:04:22.756 --> 00:04:25.545
find more talent, they have to bring me,

00:04:25.545 --> 00:04:27.998
I have to get a mix tape from them,

00:04:27.998 --> 00:04:30.245
I need to know what music
they're listening to

00:04:30.245 --> 00:04:32.670
'cause taste in music
tells a lot about a person.

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:34.528
It really does.

00:04:34.528 --> 00:04:37.719
I got to know who their
favorite designer is.

00:04:37.719 --> 00:04:41.203
What's the last book they
read, favorite artist.

00:04:41.203 --> 00:04:44.161
And it's funny, 'cause sometimes
you get those (laughs),

00:04:44.161 --> 00:04:45.937
the answers are hilarious

00:04:45.937 --> 00:04:47.613
but people be trying, you know,

00:04:47.613 --> 00:04:49.903
but you honestly have to have,

00:04:49.903 --> 00:04:52.975
I look for all your
senses to be activated,

00:04:52.975 --> 00:04:54.617
you know what I mean?

00:04:54.617 --> 00:04:56.499
I need you to have good taste in music,

00:04:56.499 --> 00:04:58.023
I need you to have work ethic,

00:04:58.023 --> 00:04:59.743
I need you to be a good person,

00:04:59.743 --> 00:05:01.755
I need you to have good taste in clothes.

00:05:01.755 --> 00:05:05.116
You need to be able to be savvy
in more than just one thing.

00:05:05.116 --> 00:05:07.214
Everyone in my staff can do, like,

00:05:07.214 --> 00:05:10.028
there's not one job that
anyone does in my staff.

00:05:10.028 --> 00:05:12.987
If I make a regular business
that doesn't touch pop culture

00:05:12.987 --> 00:05:15.226
and doesn't make history,
then, to some people,

00:05:15.226 --> 00:05:16.558
that would be considered going backwards.

00:05:16.558 --> 00:05:17.680
That's not a pressure for me

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:19.572
because I could care
less what people think.

00:05:19.572 --> 00:05:21.579
I don't think there's
anything about my career,

00:05:21.579 --> 00:05:23.399
where you would think I
did it for someone else.

00:05:23.399 --> 00:05:25.337
I'm just constantly
trying to impress myself.

00:05:25.337 --> 00:05:28.612
I've accomplished, relatively
speaking, a lot of things.

00:05:28.612 --> 00:05:29.591
And because of that,

00:05:29.591 --> 00:05:31.960
I've been able to do
exactly what inspires me.

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:33.885
Everyone has the ability
to take care of themselves.

00:05:33.885 --> 00:05:35.440
You can always be a hunter,

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:37.449
you can always eat the food you kill.

00:05:37.449 --> 00:05:39.373
It's just about how lazy you are.

00:05:39.373 --> 00:05:40.635
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:40.635 --> 00:05:41.588
Period.

00:05:41.588 --> 00:05:43.260
It's all about your effort.

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:45.153
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:05:45.153 --> 00:05:45.986
I hope you enjoyed.

00:05:45.986 --> 00:05:47.683
